r-one-price each; next tier-two-count copies at tier-two-price eac | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"d07b9099-b35a-3342-a1fa-b46bd85f3764\"}\n- language-cell [known]: (define name expression) binds a cell. (network [parameters] body) creates a callable. A network body can contain local define forms and return its final expres | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"835ea109-0649-36e3-9558-65410a50c4cd\"}\n- context-cell [known]: One worker and lexical child remain alive throughout the questions. Earlier definitions remain available in the binding directory. written-code and history cont | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"949dd17b-c2fa-35d3-9cba-303ce8ab37f2\"}\n- output-format-cell [known]: Read phase first. In analysis phase, return ONLY one EDN map, no Markdown or executable forms, with nonempty string fields :outputs :facts :unknowns :units :rul | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"f8f97a3b-62de-378d-83ba-90e94d318132\"}\n- role-cell [known]: Work carefully from the problem and available facts. Follow the strict procedure and the response format for the current phase. The implementation source is adm | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"4e8d5fa9-4ac4-314d-8926-28aa46340646\"}\n- analysis-record [known]: {:tests \"Use known boundary examples and check the pricing rules\", :branches \"Inspect rush, membership, discount cap and delivery threshold\", :rules \"Apply the  | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"d4855f7d-08f0-32c8-a713-1744dc6572c7\"}\n- phase [known]: implementation | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"cdd0b161-853d-3b81-81ae-033bfdc6b968\"}"} {:id "analysis-2", :text "# Live environment\n\n## phase\nanalysis\n\n## analysis-record\nNo analysis has been submitted for this question yet.\n\n## role-cell\nWork carefully from the problem and available facts. Follow the strict procedure and the response format for the current phase. The implementation source is admitted into one persistent lexical child.\n\n## procedure-cell\nStrict procedure, used on its own in this experiment. ANALYSIS phase: Before constructing a solution, (1) ground the problem: identify requested outputs, supplied facts, unknowns, units, applicable rules and relevant branches; (2) inspect available bindings and earlier source for relevant callable operators, checking parameters, outputs, assumptions and dependencies rather than names alone; (3) choose an approach: use a suitable existing operator with the current inputs; if none fits, explain the gap and decide whether to adapt an operator or construct one with explicit parameters. Return a concise structured analysis and operator-selection record. Do not implement yet. IMPLEMENTATION phase: implement the recorded approach, using the current inputs. Test it against the original rules with checks capable of exposing a mistake; repeating the implementation arithmetic is not an independent check. Keep new callable operators available. This procedure does not prescribe task-specific formulas or which operator to create.\n\n## output-format-cell\nRead phase first. In analysis phase, return ONLY one EDN map, no Markdown or executable forms, with nonempty string fields :outputs :facts :unknowns :units :rules :branches :operators :operator :tests, plus :decision equal to :reuse, :adapt, or :construct. Use \"none\" for unknowns or operator when appropriate. :operators must summarize the candidates actually available and their suitability. :operator names the selected existing callable for reuse/adapt or proposed new callable for construct. :tests describes independent tests and what mistakes they could detect. The host checks record completeness and existence of selected reuse/adapt callables, not the correctness of your analysis. In implementation phase, analysis-record contains your unchanged analysis. Return executable Lain source only, without fences. Existing parent ports must be connected, not redefined. order-N and pricing are input structs; quote-N has :production :rush :discount :subtotal :delivery :tax :total. Connect the computed breakdown to those slots, a text reply to user-output-N, and your test outcome to self-check-N. N is the current round. Use Lain operations on inputs, not precomputed answer constants. Only final total is rounded to cents.\n\n## context-cell\nOne worker and lexical child remain alive throughout the questions. Earlier definitions remain available in the binding directory. written-code and history contain actual prior source and user/reply messages. Return new forms for the current ask. You may construct test cases or consistency checks using the available operators and connect a boolean result to self-check-N. The parent supplies no quote formula or solved example.\n\n## language-cell\n(define name expression) binds a cell. (network [parameters] body) creates a callable. A network body can contain local define forms and return its final expression, including a struct. (struct :key value ...) constructs connected fields. Read a field with ((slot :key) object). Write an existing field with (-> computed-value ((slot :key) output-object)). + - * / min max >= <= = str and round-money are support-aware operations. (select condition then-value else-value) selects a branch. round-money rounds to two decimals, half up; use it only on the final amount. str builds text from connected values. Unknown inputs leave dependent computations unresolved. ttms-premise-closure attaches a premise to a callable; invocation carries it to results. Example: (define f (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) some-premise)). inspect:premises accepts (cell:reference binding). The struct operators and primitive documentation are capabilities, not prebuilt pricing solutions.\n\n## rules-cell\nFictional print-shop rules: progressive production pricing: first tier-one-limit copies at tier-one-price each; next tier-two-count copies at tier-two-price each; remaining copies at tier-three-price each. Rush service adds rush-rate times production cost. Members receive member-rate times production plus rush charges as discount, capped by the order discount-cap; nonmembers receive no discount. Add setup-fee after discount. Delivery costs delivery-fee, waived when subtotal after discount and setup is at least free-delivery-threshold. Apply tax-rate to the entire amount including delivery. Final total includes tax and is rounded half up to cents; intermediate values are not rounded.\n\n## metadata-cell\npricing exposes the shared numeric rules. Every order-N contains independently supported :quantity, :rush? boolean, :member? boolean, :discount-cap, and :question premise. question premises identify the corresponding requested quote. shared-rule identifies the validity premise for the general pricing rules. Keep independent orders separate. A promotional discount-cap belongs only to the order carrying it. delivery-note is unrelated. Quote output slots are production cost, rush charge, discount amount, subtotal after setup, delivery charge, tax amount, and final rounded total. Future orders are unknown until asked.\n\n## ask\nQuote 240 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total.\n\n## written-code\n[\"(define quote-fn\\n (ttms-premise-closure\\n  (network [o p]\\n   (define qty ((slot :quantity) o))\\n   (define first-count (min qty ((slot :tier-one-limit) p)))\\n   (define remaining (max 0 (- qty first-count)))\\n   (define second-count (min remaining ((slot :tier-two-count) p)))\\n   (define third-count (max 0 (- remaining second-count)))\\n   (define production (+ (* first-count ((slot :tier-one-price) p)) (* second-count ((slot :tier-two-price) p)) (* third-count ((slot :tier-three-price) p))))\\n   (define rush (select ((slot :rush?) o) (* production ((slot :rush-rate) p)) 0))\\n   (define discount (select ((slot :member?) o) (min (* (+ production rush) ((slot :member-rate) p)) ((slot :discount-cap) o)) 0))\\n   (define subtotal (+ (- (+ production rush) discount) ((slot :setup-fee) p)))\\n   (define delivery (select (>= subtotal ((slot :free-delivery-threshold) p)) 0 ((slot :delivery-fee) p)))\\n   (define tax (* (+ subtotal delivery) ((slot :tax-rate) p)))\\n   (define total (round-money (+ subtotal delivery tax)))\\n   (struct :production production :rush rush :discount discount :subtotal subtotal :delivery delivery :tax tax :total total))\\n  shared-rule))\\n(define q1 ((ttms-premise-closure quote-fn question-1) order-1 pricing))\\n(-> ((slot :production) q1) ((slot :production) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :rush) q1) ((slot :rush) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :discount) q1) ((slot :discount) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :subtotal) q1) ((slot :subtotal) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :delivery) q1) ((slot :delivery) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :tax) q1) ((slot :tax) quote-1))\\n(-> ((slot :total) q1) ((slot :total) quote-1))\\n(-> (str \\\"Total: \\\" ((slot :total) q1)) user-output-1)\\n(-> (= ((slot :total) q1) (round-money (+ ((slot :subtotal) q1) ((slot :delivery) q1) ((slot :tax) q1)))) self-check-1)\\n\"]\n\n## history\n[{:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 80 copies for a nonmember using standard service. Show the charges and final total.\"} {:role \"assistant\", :content \"Total: 212.76\"} {:role \"user\", :content \"Quote 240 copies for a member using rush service. Show the charges and final total.\"}]\n\n## Binding directory\n- q1 [known]: compound; inspect its immediate slots | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"06ab0468-69be-3f61-84ba-52da4cb6a830\"}\n- quote-fn [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"62f2897e-1bd1-3cc9-a6ac-67295f805562\"}\n- inspect:premises [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction-cell | reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"f3cafb7e-9825-334a-9404-100d70bcc84b\"}\n- cell:reference [known]: callable; inspect the binding and language-introduction